From: Jack Kingston <998656+jkingston@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] build: disable obsolete TKIP for the Brick station

The Brick product supports open networks and WPA2-PSK with CCMP.  Its XR829
firmware can remain joined but unable to scan after attempting a WPA/TKIP BSS,
and TKIP is obsolete cryptography outside the product security scope.

Build out TKIP so mixed WPA/WPA2 access points can still negotiate their CCMP
RSN mode, while TKIP-only profiles are rejected before the driver mutates
firmware state.  WEP is already absent because CONFIG_WEP is opt-in.

Signed-off-by: Jack Kingston <998656+jkingston@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 wpa_supplicant/defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/wpa_supplicant/defconfig
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/defconfig
@@ -658,7 +658,7 @@
 # use WPA+WPA2 mixed mode. For now, the default wpa_supplicant build includes
 # support for this by default, but that functionality is subject to be removed
 # in the future.
-#CONFIG_NO_TKIP=y
+CONFIG_NO_TKIP=y
 
 # Pre-Association Security Negotiation (PASN)
 #CONFIG_PASN=y
